<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani banks to close on Friday's holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistani banks to close on Friday's holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks and financial institutions in Pakistan will remain closed on Friday, which will be an Islamic religious holiday to mark the birthday of the prophet Mohammad, bankers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>An official of the State (central) Bank of Pakistan said the bank would remain closed for public business on Friday owing to the Eid Milad-un-Nabi holiday.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
